{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And at that time</b> — then the day comes and the time arrives of which he said: \"until thrones were set in place and the Ancient of Days took His seat\" (Daniel 7:9). And we cannot interpret, for <b>Michael will stand up</b> as standing alone — rather he stood only to cast down the thrones of the kings of Ishmael. And the proof is the verse after it: <b>who stands over the children of your people</b>. And <b>this trouble</b> will be upon <b>all the world</b>, and they will not escape — only because Michael is the great prince over Israel, therefore <b>your people will escape</b>, <b>everyone who is found written in the book</b>, and they are the righteous. As it is written: \"And a book of remembrance was written before Him for those who fear HaShem\" (Malachi 3:16)."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The comment contains a long run-on chain typical of Ibn Ezra's compressed style; the syntax has been preserved without inserting connective tissue."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:26.940974526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}